*Cloud-Based ETL Data Engineering Pipeline

A production-style cloud data engineering project that demonstrates how raw data can be extracted, cleaned, transformed, stored, and prepared for downstream analytics using Python and AWS.

*Project Overview

This project implements an end-to-end ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) pipeline designed to process raw datasets and convert them into clean, structured, analysis-ready data.

The pipeline demonstrates practical data engineering concepts including:

- Data extraction
- Data validation
- Data cleaning
- Data transformation
- Data quality checks
- Cloud storage
- ETL automation
- Python-based data processing
- AWS cloud infrastructure

The project was designed as a hands-on demonstration of how a data pipeline can move data from a raw state to a structured state suitable for analytics and reporting.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture

```text
                    ┌──────────────────┐
                    │   Raw Dataset    │
                    └────────┬─────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
                    ┌──────────────────┐
                    │     Extract      │
                    │     Python       │
                    └────────┬─────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
                    ┌──────────────────┐
                    │      Clean       │
                    │   & Validate     │
                    └────────┬─────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
                    ┌──────────────────┐
                    │    Transform     │
                    │     Python       │
                    └────────┬─────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
                    ┌──────────────────┐
                    │     AWS S3       │
                    │  Cloud Storage   │
                    └────────┬─────────┘
                             │
                             ▼
                    ┌──────────────────┐
                    │ Processed Data   │
                    │   & Analytics    │
                    └──────────────────┘
